# What this repo takes from ANTfrastructure. One row per asset: the id from
# third_party/ANTfrastructure/shared/config/shared-assets.manifest, and a path only
# when the copy does not sit at that registry row's default.
#
# Checked by:
#   bash third_party/ANTfrastructure/shared/config/sync-shared-config.sh --repo-root . --check
#
# THE THREE DELIBERATE OVERRIDES. This repo carries all five shared configs but
# takes only two of them. The other three are this project's own answer to a
# real problem and are NOT drift; leaving them out of this file is how that is
# declared, and this comment is the record of why. Re-adding a row below would
# make the gate demand the canonical file and erase the reason.
#
#   .clang-tidy              adds `-clang-diagnostic-error` and a
#                            HeaderFilterRegex ('^Src/.*\.h(pp)?$|^Src/.*\.ixx$').
#                            Both answer clang-tidy seeing an `import` without
#                            the BMIs on the command line. BeschleunigerBallett
#                            answers the same question by skipping module TUs
#                            instead (Test-IsCxxModuleTranslationUnit). Two valid
#                            strategies; forcing either on the other weakens it.
#   gcovr.cfg                the coverage excludes follow THIS layout -
#                            third_party, .*_deps, resources (lower-case here),
#                            plus an `exclude` regex the canonical file has no
#                            equivalent of.
#   .pre-commit-config.yaml  runs an extra local `clang-tidy` hook on commit.
#                            Which hooks a project runs locally is a workflow
#                            choice. NOTE: its cmake-format hook still matches
#                            `\.cmake$` only, so CMakeLists.txt is not formatted
#                            on commit here - the canonical hook was widened on
#                            2026-09-06 and this copy predates it. That half is
#                            staleness rather than intent; see shared/config/README.md.
#
# `.clang-format` is NOT an override: it was ahead of canonical, and canonical
# was corrected to match on 2026-08-11.

clang-format
cmake-format
antfrastructure-sh
resolve-build-module
